# TODO.md sync

After implementing features, finishing substantial code changes, or completing roadmap items, check whether root [`TODO.md`](TODO.md) still reflects reality — then update it in the same session.

## When to check

- New or completed feature, plugin, or product capability
- Status of an existing roadmap item clearly changed (done / partial / cancelled)
- Renames or replacements of concepts listed in TODO (e.g. Maps → Collections)
- Work that closes or advances a checkbox under P0–P3 or “Technische schuld”

Skip for tiny refactors, typo fixes, pure formatting, or changes with no product/roadmap impact.

## What to update

1. Flip checkboxes: `[ ]` → `[~]` / `[x]` (or reopen if something was removed).
2. Adjust short status text next to `[~]` items so remaining gaps stay accurate.
3. Add missing capabilities to “Huidige sterke punten” when they become real product strengths.
4. Refresh the header date (`laatst bijgewerkt`) when you edit the file.
5. Keep the Dutch style and legend (`[x]` klaar · `[~]` deels · `[ ]` open).

## Workflow

1. Skim the TODO sections that relate to the change.
2. Verify claims against the code (don’t mark done from memory alone).
3. Edit only the affected bullets — don’t rewrite the whole roadmap.
4. Mention the TODO.md update briefly in the final response when you changed it.
